#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162528 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f2a5391-d8bb-5084-941a-bb787e8729f3" :knowledge-point/title "Changing Variables in a Quadratic Form Given New Variables Through Old Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e90e13d-81be-55d4-bfa4-5429578c7c9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{1}^{2} + y_{1}y_{2} - y_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160801} {:answer/id #uuid "9c452e3c-d682-5cab-a127-d3b252ee25fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{1}^{2} + 5y_{1}y_{2} - 2y_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160802} {:answer/id #uuid "fb05c91f-fd31-58ac-87f8-6804abf1a91c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{1}^{2} - y_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160803} {:answer/id #uuid "3599299a-c360-53ca-9da7-30cb897366aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{1}^{2} - 3y_{1}y_{2} + y_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160804} {:answer/id #uuid "5e68a126-f4ea-5f53-a822-665d5d355fda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{1}^{2} - 2y_{1}y_{2} + y_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e90e13d-81be-55d4-bfa4-5429578c7c9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{1}^{2} + y_{1}y_{2} - y_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160801} :answer-field/id #uuid "e20492bb-5a47-5304-b6b1-3d36fad85e3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160800}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9c51ecf1-6711-57f2-8c41-d6bd2fed54f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-93735" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n express the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}$ in terms of the components of $y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\ngives the following expressions for ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & ={x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy solving the second equation for ${x}_{2}$ and substituting it into the first equation, we obtain the following expressions for ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={y}_{1}+2{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute these into our quadratic form expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}+2{y}_{2})^{2}+3({y}_{1}+2{y}_{2})(-{y}_{2})+(-{y}_{2})^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{1}^{2}+4{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+4{y}_{2}^{2}-3{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-6{y}_{2}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162547 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f2a5391-d8bb-5084-941a-bb787e8729f3" :knowledge-point/title "Changing Variables in a Quadratic Form Given New Variables Through Old Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea286781-dcc6-5808-99f1-2dce1ca57f4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{1}^{2} + y_{1}y_{2} + y_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160915} {:answer/id #uuid "2f5288e2-c140-5d37-b03e-24540115b45a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y_{1}^{2} + y_{1}y_{2} + y_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160916} {:answer/id #uuid "44310c62-b83d-52b0-b6b1-8695701b69d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{1}^{2} - 2y_{1}y_{2} + y_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160917} {:answer/id #uuid "631219d4-15cb-5ca1-867a-20ba2494d203" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-y_{1}^{2} - 2y_{1}y_{2} - y_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160918} {:answer/id #uuid "68c62326-bbef-5cbe-9955-33307532e827" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2y_{1}^{2} - y_{1}y_{2} + y_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68c62326-bbef-5cbe-9955-33307532e827" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2y_{1}^{2} - y_{1}y_{2} + y_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160919} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ab404f4-6cb2-55ca-8df4-204303d94851" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160914}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "28be3e2f-b0ff-5855-af78-c4f12425ac89" :question/math-academy-id "q-94180" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n express the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}$ in terms of the components of $y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\ngives the following expressions for ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & ={x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving these for ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =-{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} & ={y}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute these into our quadratic form expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =(-{y}_{2})^{2}+(-{y}_{2}){y}_{1}-2{y}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{2}{y}_{1}-2{y}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-2{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376233 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "331cb610-6168-5161-b821-237c713dedaa" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Quadratic Form Given a Change-of-Coordinates Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c24f5bda-215d-5ccf-9cec-040154c96e54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 25 \\\\ 25 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376235} {:answer/id #uuid "defd1f32-35bd-5421-b361-7cf2b9c1b71b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 & 16 \\\\ 16 & 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376236} {:answer/id #uuid "2909b54e-42ae-5da0-b933-44328dd00ba3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}11 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376237} {:answer/id #uuid "6389fd0c-d3b8-5052-8107-67733391b421" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}21 & 26 \\\\ 26 & 32\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376238} {:answer/id #uuid "f53a6c78-1e79-50fa-a49f-589cd37609fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 & 15 \\\\ 15 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376239}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6389fd0c-d3b8-5052-8107-67733391b421" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}21 & 26 \\\\ 26 & 32\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376238} :answer-field/id #uuid "720abd7a-75d5-567c-827e-a8a90b77fa21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376234}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "89a8b501-1e1d-5651-8ffd-47612aef6ccf" :question/math-academy-id "q-94182" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $P$ above. Find the matrix of the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in the basis that consists of the columns of $P.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $x=[{x}_{1},{x}_{2}]^{T}$ is a vector given by its coordinates in the standard basis and $y=[{y}_{1},{y}_{2}]^{T}$ is the same vector but given in the coordinates relative to the basis that consists of the columns of $P,$ then \n\n$$\nx=Py.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =(Py)^{T}\\,A\\,(Py) \\\\  & =({y}^{T}{P}^{T})\\,A\\,(Py) \\\\  & ={y}^{T}({P}^{T}\\,AP)\\,y,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that the matrix of our form in the new basis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{T}\\,AP & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 5 \\\\ 10 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}21 & 26 \\\\ 26 & 32\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376240 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "331cb610-6168-5161-b821-237c713dedaa" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Quadratic Form Given a Change-of-Coordinates Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30c2ab12-6b74-570d-bc81-d699ba963f40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}27 & 15 \\\\ 15 & 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376242} {:answer/id #uuid "2c1d776a-5292-5fba-8ef7-b081cb8ff082" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376243} {:answer/id #uuid "e8df4f73-746d-5651-97bc-7dee7f8fc7b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 & 20 \\\\ 20 & 11\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376244} {:answer/id #uuid "7b003303-3562-52f2-a40e-491ed273eaa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}27 & 20 \\\\ 20 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376245} {:answer/id #uuid "2ee424b9-7a3e-5f0a-bbd0-cac781ee1f6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}47 & 30 \\\\ 30 & 19\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376246}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ee424b9-7a3e-5f0a-bbd0-cac781ee1f6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}47 & 30 \\\\ 30 & 19\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376246} :answer-field/id #uuid "ded6bca5-ca72-553a-9441-53e2afe8cad0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376241}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fb87dad8-da1e-5ede-8c9c-d17d9f1877cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-94183" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $P$ above. Find the matrix of the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in the basis that consists of the columns of $P.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $x=[{x}_{1},{x}_{2}]^{T}$ is a vector given by its coordinates in the standard basis and $y=[{y}_{1},{y}_{2}]^{T}$ is the same vector but given in the coordinates relative to the basis that consists of the columns of $P,$ then \n\n$$\nx=Py.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =(Py)^{T}\\,A\\,(Py) \\\\  & =({y}^{T}{P}^{T})\\,A\\,(Py) \\\\  & ={y}^{T}({P}^{T}\\,AP)\\,y,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that the matrix of our form in the new basis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{T}\\,AP & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 13 \\\\ 3 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}47 & 30 \\\\ 30 & 19\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376247 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "331cb610-6168-5161-b821-237c713dedaa" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Quadratic Form Given a Change-of-Coordinates Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bcd7bf6-273c-5c87-9490-a6c6f0b67c1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376249} {:answer/id #uuid "ace819de-f5b0-583e-94b5-900f338981a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376250} {:answer/id #uuid "3424bfc8-2f29-5456-975c-8242782987bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376251} {:answer/id #uuid "8f563111-4bd5-5354-983b-04cd2329631e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376252} {:answer/id #uuid "c595fdfb-1ae0-5d9d-b225-66141f9258a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376253}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2bcd7bf6-273c-5c87-9490-a6c6f0b67c1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376249} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1f7d2ee-49d5-5c11-86ad-2a2114339a81" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376248}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8cb11b26-b52b-5b61-9570-f38af34aa8e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-94187" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & \\,\\,-2\\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}\\,-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & \\,\\,-2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $P$ above. Find the matrix of the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in the basis that consists of the columns of $P.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $x=[{x}_{1},{x}_{2}]^{T}$ is a vector given by its coordinates in the standard basis and $y=[{y}_{1},{y}_{2}]^{T}$ is the same vector but given in the coordinates relative to the basis that consists of the columns of $P,$ then \n\n$$\nx=Py.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =(Py)^{T}\\,A\\,(Py) \\\\  & =({y}^{T}{P}^{T})\\,A\\,(Py) \\\\  & ={y}^{T}({P}^{T}\\,AP)\\,y,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that the matrix of our form in the new basis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{T}\\,AP & ={[\\begin{aligned}\\,-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & \\,\\,-2\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & \\,\\,-2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\,-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & \\,\\,-2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & \\,\\,-2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & \\,\\,-2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\,-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & \\,\\,-2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\,-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & \\,\\,-2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
